2), per the triage-scoped packet: the agreement checker, with the Phase 2-3 disagreements explicit as waivers. Issue #7089 stays open for Phases 2-4.\n\n- Tier-to-trigger mapping written into .github/ci-policy.md: PR (basic) tier = pull_request trigger; main tier = push to main or a named equivalent venue; nightly = schedule. workflow_dispatch-only satisfies no tier, and merge_group satisfies no tier after Drews 2026-11-08 no-merge-queue ruling (recorded in ci-policy; supersedes the designs original merge_group pin).\n- production-line-guards missing tier row added to the ci-policy tier table.\n- New checker .github/scripts/check-ci-policy-agreement.sh wired into workflow-lint (plus its contract tests): for every in-scope workflow, tier, declared triggers, and the recorded waiver set must agree. Unwaived disagreements fail naming the workflow and leg; waivers whose leg now agrees fail as stale; a vanished ci-policy row or workflow file fails.\n- Waivers name their phase issues: #6929 (mcpx-fix-test-guard, PR+main legs), #6953 (opencode-config-guard, main leg; venue disabled_manually), #6959 (production-line-guard, PR leg), #6981 (four build workflows, PR+main legs; venues disabled_manually). Checker on this tree: 10 workflows checked, 12 waived legs, OK.\n- No workflow re-armed, re-enabled, or trigger-changed (workflow-lint gains the checker steps and the ci-policy/checker paths only).\n\nTests (oracle: the agreement contract): contract tests cover the waived-set pass, unwaived disagreement, stale waiver, missing policy row, and missing workflow file — all pass locally; the checker itself is green on this tree.\n\nRefs #7089\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796789027&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7945&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7945&signature=59ac4b356157102c77274679503cae68c8eb33dec0de